※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4644

※ A lambda kept in `⎕heap` has a type saying it lasts as long as the program,
※ so what it brought in has to last as well.  A lambda a parameter that says
※ nothing was handed may keep what it brought in in the caller's frame.

fn wrapped(g: fn(u8) → u8) → fn(u8) in ⎕heap → u8:
    λ x: u8 [g] in ⎕heap → u8 { g(x) }

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
